# RiftNest VPN bundle — connect in 3 steps

## 1. Install files
```bash
mkdir -p ~/.ssh
cp vpnuser-key ~/.ssh/riftnest-vpnuser-key
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/riftnest-vpnuser-key
# append ssh_config to your SSH config:
cat ssh_config >> ~/.ssh/config
```

## 2. Open the SSH forward (carries OpenVPN through the hosting edge)
```bash
ssh -f -N riftnest-vpn
```

## 3. Start OpenVPN through it
```bash
sudo openvpn --config riftnest-client2.ovpn
```

## Verify
```bash
ping -c 2 10.0.2.1   # VPN server
ping -c 2 10.0.3.1   # container bridge — each container gets its own 10.0.3.x
```

## Notes
- `vpnuser` can ONLY open the port-1194 forward. No shell, no password, nothing else.
- `riftnest-client2.ovpn` points at `127.0.0.1:1194` on purpose — that is the
  local end of the SSH forward, not the real server address.
- Keep `vpnuser-key` private. One bundle per person; ask the admin for your
  own client cert if you need one.
